		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: Organizing My Saved Repeaters in GD77 Using CSV Export/Import]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4922&amp;p=36002#p36002"><![CDATA[
When moving channels in channels.csv you must copy the entire row of data and make sure the columns remain aligned. If creating a new channel it is best to copy the row of a similar channel and then make changes to the columns as needed. Always ensure the channel number column is unique. Two channels with the same channel number will overwrite each other.  Channel numbers don't have to be sequential (they can have gaps) but they must be unique. <br><br>The CPS should automatically cope with commas or periods based on the windows country settings. It also scans input lines and tries to identify the format automatically. <br><br>Yes, you can create new zones and add channels to them, just add an extra line to zones.csv and make sure the channel names in the columns are exactly the same as those defined in channels.csv. <br><br>Internally the Code plug uses index numbers to refer to channels, zones, contacts etc. <br>The CSV builds these indexes from the names used in the CSV files using exact matching.  So it is important that the names are exactly the same wherever they are used. <br><br>Colin G4EML<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=87">G4EML</a> — Fri Feb 28, 2025 12:47 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
